Component By Component
1. ServiceNow

Purpose:

Request starts here


Examples:

Change Request
Incident
Service Request
Task

ServiceNow decides:

Can this automation run?
Does it require approval?
Who approved it?


Then sends request to AAP.

2. AAP (Ansible Automation Platform)

This is the brain.

Purpose:

Execute automation


Examples:

Interface shutdown
VLAN creation
BGP modification
Self-healing incident
New user provisioning

Everything is executed by AAP playbooks.

3. GitHub

Purpose:

Store automation code
Store configurations
Version Control


Think:

GitHub = Source Code Library


Whenever somebody changes automation:

Old Version
      ↓
New Version
      ↓
Review
      ↓
Audit Trail


Everything becomes traceable.

4. NSoT (Network Source of Truth)

This is the MOST IMPORTANT NEW COMPONENT.

Purpose:

Single truth of network


Stores:

Device inventory
IP information
Topology
Golden configuration
Site information
Model numbers
Serial numbers

Document explicitly says:

NSoT = Authoritative Data Source


Meaning:

If NSoT says VLAN = 100

Then everybody trusts that value.

Why NSoT Is Needed?

Without NSoT:

Excel Sheet A
Excel Sheet B
CMDB
Engineer Notes
Random Documents

Nobody knows truth


With NSoT:

One place
One source
One truth

